.TH GFXTUNE 1 2026-11-07 "gfxtune @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gfxtune \- graphics and game tuning for Steam games
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfxtune
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfxtune
sets graphics options for all Steam games and for each game: anisotropic
filtering, texture detail, vertical sync, a frame cap, FSR\~4, gamescope,
GameMode, MangoHud, and in\-game filters (anti\-aliasing, sharpening and
colour) drawn by its Vulkan layer. It also measures each play session and
shows the graphics card's temperatures, power, clocks and load.
.PP
Settings reach a game through
.BR gfxtune\-run (1),
which gfxtune puts into the game's Steam launch options, before
.BR %command% ,
while Steam is closed. Without an option,
.B gfxtune
opens its window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-games
Print the Steam games gfxtune finds and what it reads about each: how it
runs (native or which Proton), the graphics libraries it loads, FSR\~3.1,
anti\-cheat, and its current launch options. Only reads; nothing is changed.
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-launch\-lines
Take
.B gfxtune\-run
out of every game's Steam launch options. Refuses while Steam is running,
because Steam writes its settings back when it exits. The package does this
for every user before gfxtune is removed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gfxtune/global.ini
The settings for all games.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gfxtune/games/APPID.ini
One game's own changes to them, whether it uses them at all, an accepted
anti\-cheat warning, and the anti\-cheat gfxtune found in the game.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gfxtune/last\-launch/
What
.B gfxtune\-run
applied at each game's last start, and what the layer reported from inside it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gfxtune/performance/APPID/
Each game's measured play sessions.
.PP
gfxtune reads Steam's files where Steam keeps them and only ever changes
the launch options of
.IR localconfig.vdf .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STEAM_EXTRA_COMPAT_TOOLS_PATHS
More folders with Proton builds, separated by colons, as Steam reads it.
.TP
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES
Problems are logged as warnings in the categories
.BR gfxtune.steam ,
.B gfxtune.launch
and
.BR gfxtune.settings ;
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES="gfxtune.*.debug=true"
also logs what gfxtune does, such as each launch option it changes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when
.B \-\-remove\-launch\-lines
could not change Steam's settings, for example because Steam is running.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gfxtune\-run (1),
.BR gamescope (1),
.BR gamemoderun (1),
.BR mangohud (1)
